## The Mathematical Engine Behind TikTok's Ad Auction

Most media buyers believe that their CPM (Cost Per Mille impressions) on TikTok is governed solely by audience targeting, bids, and seasonality. In reality, TikTok operates on a sophisticated auction scoring mechanism where **creative quality is the dominant pricing multiplier**.

In TikTok's real-time auction, ad rank is determined by the following formula:

$$\text{eCPM} = (\text{Bid} \times P(\text{eCTR}) \times P(\text{eCVR})) \times \mathbf{CQF} + \text{Relevance Score}$$

Where:
- **$P(\text{eCTR})$**: Predicted Click-Through Rate based on early impression signals.
- **$P(\text{eCVR})$**: Predicted Conversion Rate based on historical post-click behavior.
- **$\mathbf{CQF}$ (Creative Quality Factor)**: A real-time coefficient (ranging from 0.5x to 2.5x) awarded to creatives that keep users engaged on the platform without inducing fatigue.

If your video ad captivates viewers and keeps them watching, TikTok **subsidizes your ad auction**, lowering your CPM by up to 40%. Conversely, if viewers swipe away in the first 2 seconds, TikTok imposes a heavy CPM penalty to protect user experience.

